A||N||11||danny boy||lost keys  ||||8||
Z||000000||danny boy||10-21-2001||10:36 PM|||| First off, it was a nice weekend weatherwise and I was so looking forward to getting the GT running with the new engine.<BR>   My bushings came in, I had everything I needed(for once),all the prep work on the GT was done. I gathered up all the stuff I was going to take, and then, I realized I didn't have the keys to my other car.<BR>  Great. where are they? I looked everywhere. All over my house, at my moms house and in all my cars. Nowhere to be found. Now, seeing as how my decklid is closed(no power latch), the strreing column is locked and the car is in the garage backwards I'm stuck. I can't get the decklid open to get anything done back there and the wheels are turned so I can't get them off to get the control arms I need.<BR>   So how do you open a decklid with no keys? I have junk louvers on it so I will cut them up to get to the hinge bolts if they can be taken out and the lid raised up enough to pop the lock.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_5.jpg"> ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Sage||10-21-2001||11:16 PM||||You should be able to take the VIN to the Pontiac dealer and have a key cut.  Or long way around, pop the steering wheel off snd remove the cylinder, take it to a locksmith and he should be able to cut a key from it.  Had this situation with an AMC Eagle which uses the same key for ign. and door lock.  Took the cylinder from a door in to locksmith and he cut me a new key that worked just fine.  No guarantees, but a couple suggestions.  To get in the trunk, you could also use a long blade(I mean LOOONG,like 12"!) flat head screw driver in the trunk latch.  It will ruin the latch, but it will get you in the trunk.  Any way you go...good luck!<BR>edited to add:<P>Now Roger...before you come down too hard on me, I didn't lose the keys to the Eagle, the guy I got it from didn't have them and I wanted to hear it run!  Now I could tell you about what I had to do to get a title...but that's a whole different story!LOL  You are right though, I have extra keys to everything I drive.  (They're not always where I am when I need them...but I have them!LOL     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>------------------<BR>Have a good one!<P>[This message has been edited by Sage (edited 10-21-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Sage (edited 10-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||10-21-2001||11:28 PM||||well, for the 10,000 th time, I cant figure out why people wont spend $2 for spare keys.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||3
Z||000003||Sootah||10-21-2001||11:44 PM||||I keep a spare set (with out the plastic coating, of course) in my wallet. Never locked myself out. Won't be until I don't have my spares with me that I do. <P>Damn you Murphy, damn you... Or should we thank Murphy for making the law? Without it we might not know what to expect..<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">     <BR><sup><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter</sup>||||reg||7
Z||000004||SLYGUY||10-22-2001||01:23 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>well, for the 10,000 th time, I cant figure out why people wont spend $2 for spare keys.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>And I felt stupid for getting copies made the day AFTER I bought the car. <BR>The keys may not necessarily be with me when I need them, but are on my only other keyset. I'm superstitious like that. A copy of the keys are always made. First bit of 'work' always done to the new car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000005||Red2m4||10-22-2001||02:50 PM||||<BR>I once locked my keys AND my spare keys in my fiero.  (yes, i am an idiot) thats when i had to resort to the slim-jim.  worked ok, except it ruined one of the dew strips.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula||10-22-2001||04:43 PM||||I think that every fiero owner loses the keys to their car... <P>Dan, did you get anything else done to it?<P>I have about 3 hours worth of work before mine will start up, basically I need to install the ignition.  I might wait until march to put it back under insurance now.<P>ps: you have to hear my awesome ricer mobile now with my custom intake and exhaust LOL (professionally done by me, for free!)<p>[This message has been edited by Formula (edited 10-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||danny boy||10-22-2001||05:07 PM|||| My spare set is in the trunk. I wanted to leave that part out, but Roger called me on it. I won't go into how they got in there....<BR>  Bushings and interior will be back together by the end of the week. Asuming you're not supposed to be able to push the old bushings out with your fingers, I'd say I was long overdue for these.<BR>   ||||reg||1
