Z||000009||GT-maniac||10-23-2001||12:16 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by danny boy:<BR><B> First off, it was a nice weekend weatherwise and I was so looking forward to getting the GT running with the new engine.<BR>   My bushings came in, I had everything I needed(for once),all the prep work on the GT was done. I gathered up all the stuff I was going to take, and then, I realized I didn't have the keys to my other car.<BR>  Great. where are they? I looked everywhere. All over my house, at my moms house and in all my cars. Nowhere to be found. Now, seeing as how my decklid is closed(no power latch), the strreing column is locked and the car is in the garage backwards I'm stuck. I can't get the decklid open to get anything done back there and the wheels are turned so I can't get them off to get the control arms I need.<BR>   So how do you open a decklid with no keys? I have junk louvers on it so I will cut them up to get to the hinge bolts if they can be taken out and the lid raised up enough to pop the lock.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Try using the door key from your other fiero first. I've replaced both decklid locks on my 85 and 87 cars and they have different keys of course. But I can use the door key from either car to unlock the decklid on either car. Must be those quality GM locks I guess, they're not too picky.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero005a.jpg">  <P>85 WS6 GT partly modified<BR>87 GT Loaded resto project<p>[This message has been edited by GT-maniac (edited 10-23-2001).]||||reg||1
